# Scripts that run under Linux must be checked out with LF line endings. GitHub workflow steps
# source them under `bash -e`, and the executor image executes its entrypoint directly: with CRLF
# the kernel resolves the interpreter as "sh" plus a carriage return, so the entrypoint cannot
# start and a sourced file fails at "set: pipefail" plus a carriage return before it creates any
# fixture. Everything else in this Windows-first repository keeps its committed line endings;
# tests/structural/test_line_endings.py enforces the rule on the files themselves.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
